-- ... the ceiling, once S$800 and four merchants are met: additive 10 + 350 = 360; replacement 10 + 260 = 270.
#ASSERT (`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a fresh yuu month`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 360
#ASSERT elem `yuu: S$800 of Eligible Spend and four Participating Merchants by month end` ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a fresh yuu month`)'s `depends on`)
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a fresh yuu month`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... 0.28 miles per yuu Point "or more": the certain miles are 100 x 0.28 = 28.
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a fresh yuu month`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 28
-- ... the cash value: 100 yuu Points x S$0.005 = S$0.50.
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a fresh yuu month`)'s `cash value certain`) EQUALS 0.5
-- ... the pot named.
#ASSERT (`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a fresh yuu month`)'s pot EQUALS `yuu bonus`

-- cl.7(b): the minimum is met by this purchase. S$790 so far with three merchants, S$20 at foodpanda (the fourth):
-- S$810 and four merchants. Additive: Base 20 + 35 x 20 = 720; replacement: 20 + 26 x 20 = 540. Floor 540, ceiling 720.
#ASSERT (`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 540
#ASSERT (`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 720
-- ... the minimum condition is no longer named, but the stacking fork is.
#ASSERT NOT (elem `yuu: S$800 of Eligible Spend and four Participating Merchants by month end` ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants`)'s `depends on`))
#ASSERT elem `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)` ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... Cold Storage, CS Fresh and Jasons Deli are ONE Participating Merchant: with them and Giant that is two, not four.
#ASSERT `the number of Participating Merchants among` (LIST `Cold Storage`, `CS Fresh`, `Jasons Deli`, `Giant`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the number of Participating Merchants among` (LIST `Cold Storage`, `Cold Storage`, `Giant`, `Guardian`, `7-Eleven`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the number of Participating Merchants among` (LIST `SingtelShop!`, `Singtel Exclusive Retailer`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of Participating Merchants among` (LIST `Another merchant`, `Netflix`) EQUALS 0
-- ... so S$20 at foodpanda on that month (three brands + foodpanda = three: Cold Storage group counts once) does not meet it.
#ASSERT elem `yuu: S$800 of Eligible Spend and four Participating Merchants by month end` ((`DBS yuu earns on` `the yuu Visa` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants and a Cold Storage group`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... S$800 alone is not enough: S$790 + S$10 = S$800 but at Cold Storage (already hit) the merchants stay at three.
#ASSERT `the Minimum Spend Requirement is met with` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Minimum Spend Requirement is met with` `S$10 at Cold Storage` `a yuu month at S$790 with three merchants`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Minimum Spend Requirement is met with` `S$20 at foodpanda` `a fresh yuu month`)

